%[text] %[text:anchor:T_78DB6566] # Biosciences: Genetics
%[text] In this module, we will learn how to use MATLAB® to analyze genetic data. We will **calculate the statistics of a single DNA sequence**, use real genetic data to **create a phylogenetic tree**, and explore **within-species genetic variation**.  This module assumes basic MATLAB knowledge and it is recommended that all students take the [MATLAB Onramp](https://matlabacademy.mathworks.com/details/matlab-onramp/gettingstarted) before continuing if they have not done so already.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_DEE5F383] ## Scripts
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_F887EB68] ### [Explore a single DNA sequence](<matlab: edit Scripts/S1ExploreSingleDNASequence.m>)
